    "version_evidence": "Official docs are unversioned. The installed exact 0.163.0 executable help independently lists app-server --listen unix://PATH and TUI --remote unix://PATH; binary digest and unmodified help outputs are retained below. This is not a claim that current docs are a frozen 0.163 manual.",
    "queue_cli_observation": "Installed codex queue --help also accepts --remote, but the proposed repair can keep the existing validated native RPC path rather than replace the protocol."
  },
  "authentication": {
    "sources": [
      "https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/auth#login-caching",
      "https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/auth#credential-storage"
    ],
    "documented_fact": "Codex reuses its cached login; file storage is under normal CODEX_HOME, default ~/.codex, or its configured OS store.",
    "proposal_inference": "Keep normal CODEX_HOME for Codex-owned authentication. Selecting a private transport does not require duplicating the credential store. The app never opens, copies or writes auth.json and never changes global config or the operator daemon.",
    "remaining_runtime_proof": "No private server was started during this read-only item. A later own-seat integration probe must confirm account availability through the normal Codex client without a login/Keychain/operator prompt; cached-login documentation is not a new live runtime proof."
  },
  "observed_failure_context": {
    "private_audit": "/var/folders/zd/mv_mr2d92p5_1r8yghzbs5vw0000gn/T/sable-codex-approve-z_kclvwr/approval-live/completed-audit.json",
    "audit_sha256": "0c3cdcb5ff7460904c03699bc7c801f3cbd40dfaf385ae4c161ad20c5266baad",
    "tuple": "requested thread equals returned thread; status notLoaded at the user-global daemon, PID 13411, while own TUI PID 94186 completes the task after a scripted start nudge",
    "read_semantics": "https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/app-server#read-a-stored-thread-without-resuming documents that thread/read reads stored data without loading/subscribing; an ID match alone is not runtime ownership.",
    "guard": "Do not accept notLoaded as idle or load/resume the thread on the operator daemon. #279 requires NativeUnknown/no retry."
  },
  "proposed_repair_order": [
    "The kit creates a neutral per-seat runtime descriptor with a short validated Unix socket in its private 0700 overlay and expresses server/TUI argv using the documented flags. Launch carries that chosen endpoint; no user-global discovery.",
    "The caller hosts the selected server for the PTY seat lifetime, surviving Logic restart and close grace. A Logic-owned background task is insufficient. Keep the kit a library with neutral descriptors, not a new dependency on mux/proto/supervisor.",
    "Record/reconstruct the selected runtime and endpoint with seat, generation, process start and native thread identity. Refresh and wake use this same endpoint only; initial binding is unavailable until the SessionStart thread rebind. Preserve normal caller hooks and MCP per-invocation overrides on the actual server/thread.",
    "Preserve exact thread and idle/active admission. A wake with notLoaded/unknown is NativeUnknown, named and stopped without retry or PTY fallback. Keep unrelated seats and messages flowing if this runtime is unavailable."
  ],
  "named_source_seams": [
    "crates/bboxy450-harness-wake-up/src/launch.rs:25 LaunchPlan and :223 Codex overlay: explicit endpoint/runtime descriptor and documented argv; preserve per-server approve and hook commands",
    "crates/bboxy450-harness-wake-up/src/lib.rs:120 Binding / :144 Endpoint: bind selected runtime identity without wire types",
    "crates/bboxy450-harness-wake-up/src/native.rs:345 codex_handshake and :410 wake: preserve identity/status guards; return typed unknown outcome for notLoaded under #279",
    "crates/bbt-mux/src/adapters/{launch,mapping}.rs: map neutral launch/runtime fields; policy and journal remain here",
    "crates/bbt-mux/src/logic.rs:3974 refresh_adapters, especially :4019-4050: replace CODEX_HOME user-global socket lookup with the retained launch-selected endpoint",
    "Seat host/launch lifecycle: exact sidecar/helper ownership must preserve the existing supervisor/PTY lifetime across Logic death; select this inside the implementation brief rather than silently making it a Logic task"
  ],
  "proposed_scripted_regressions": [
    "Kit bootstrap fixture starts unbound/process-* and non-idle; no queue mutation until the exact SessionStart bind and selected-runtime idle/active observation.",
    "A matching stored thread on an unrelated/global endpoint returning notLoaded yields NativeUnknown once, no retry and no queue/add, load/resume, steer or PTY fallback.",
    "Two seats have distinct sockets/thread bindings; one unavailable runtime does not stall the other. Exercise full failure/refusal outcomes without a single global runtime gate.",
    "Own runtime remains usable through Logic SIGKILL/restart; the selected endpoint/session is retained, and seat exit reaps its private server.",
    "Fully scripted fresh real-Codex delegation/DM -> orient -> task_report -> correlated reply/ACK without a ctl start nudge; assertion-based published-screen hook/tool recipe, no human input. Recheck foreign prompt/zero-effect negative boundary."
  ],
